  "body": "<!--\r\n⚠️ If you do not respect this template, your pull request will be closed.\r\n⚠️ Your pull request title should be short detailed and understandable for all.\r\n⚠️ Also, please add it in the CHANGELOG file under Unreleased section.\r\n⚠️ If your pull request fixes an open issue, please link to the issue.\r\n\r\n✅ I have added the tests to cover my changes.\r\n✅ I have updated the documentation accordingly.\r\n✅ I have read the CONTRIBUTING document.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR continues the work #166 by adding general improvements to the `PySCFDriver`. The others drivers will need to be tackled one-by-one in a similar fashion.\r\n\r\n### Details and comments\r\n\r\n- [x] integration of `integrals.py` as class methods\r\n- [x] improved splitting of class methods into more logical subunits\r\n- [x] updated docstrings\r\n- [x] closes #28:\r\n  - explicit checking of all input arguments is _not_ feasible\r\n  - unfortunately, PySCF also does not provide simple means to validate the arguments through some method call\r\n  - BUT, through more logical method splitting, a more meaningful error will now be raised (e.g. [this one](https://github.com/mrossinek/qiskit-nature/blob/41b2945ea572e355aace5e877a135c4a538cf904/qiskit_nature/drivers/pyscfd/pyscfdriver.py#L371))\r\n- [x] also re-evaluates #29 for this driver by updating all links to the new PySCF website (https://pyscf.org)\r\n- [x] update unittests \r\n\r\n\r\n:warning: This PR as significant conflicts with #173!",
